.SS "int32_t schultz_a11y_create (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_events\fP * events, const \fBschultz_a11y_options\fP * options, \fBschultz_a11y\fP ** out_a11y)"

.PP
Starts the bridge and publishes the tree for the first time\&. Succeeds whether or not an assistive technology is running: on Linux there may be no accessibility bus, and the right behaviour then is to sit quietly rather than to fail an application's startup\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree to describe\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIevents\fP The router, used to deliver what is asked for and to read which node has focus\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIoptions\fP Application details, or NULL for defaults\&. 
.br
\fIout_a11y\fP Receives the bridge\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT, or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

